y":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}{U}","name":"Twincast","oracle_id":"8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb","oracle_text":"Copy target instant or sorcery spell. You may choose new targets for the copy.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2009-07-17","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":3.0,"color_identity":["R"],"colors":["R"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{1}{R}{R}","name":"Volcanic Fallout","oracle_id":"bd6ce147-c991-40ac-b276-65b630fad8b6","oracle_text":"This spell can't be countered.\nVolcanic Fallout deals 2 damage to each creature and each player.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2020-11-20","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"If you don't have a commander, Arcane Signet's ability produces no mana.","oracle_id":"0bc7f093-bef0-4f1a-852c-4b75ebf54838","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you have two commanders, the ability adds one mana of any color in their combined color identities.","oracle_id":"0bc7f093-bef0-4f1a-852c-4b75ebf54838","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If your commander is a card that has no colors in its color identity, Arcane Signet's ability produces no mana. It doesn't produce {C}.","oracle_id":"0bc7f093-bef0-4f1a-852c-4b75ebf54838","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a replacement effect would try to replace a card that you can't draw, that effect can't apply.","oracle_id":"1463795b-ec0c-44d6-ae1a-55f78d9843ec","published_at":"2014-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you draw a card, and then Spirit of the Labyrinth enters the battlefield, you won't be able to draw more cards that turn.","oracle_id":"1463795b-ec0c-44d6-ae1a-55f78d9843ec","published_at":"2014-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you haven't drawn any cards in a turn, and a spell or ability would cause you to draw multiple cards, you'll just draw one card.","oracle_id":"1463795b-ec0c-44d6-ae1a-55f78d9843ec","published_at":"2014-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can draw a maximum of one card on each player's turn. Subsequent card draws are ignored.","oracle_id":"1463795b-ec0c-44d6-ae1a-55f78d9843ec","published_at":"2014-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the card has {X} in its mana cost, you must choose 0 as its value.","oracle_id":"16de96d0-a58e-42a7-9a13-45358542a246","published_at":"2011-01-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you cast a card “without paying its mana cost,” you can’t pay any alternative costs. You can pay additional costs, such as kicker costs. If the card has mandatory additional costs, you must pay those.","oracle_id":"16de96d0-a58e-42a7-9a13-45358542a246","published_at":"2011-01-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You cast the card in your hand as part of the resolution of Counterlash. Timing restrictions based on the card’s type (such as creature or sorcery) are ignored. Other restrictions are not (such as “Cast [this card] only during combat”).","oracle_id":"16de96d0-a58e-42a7-9a13-45358542a246","published_at":"2011-01-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the countered spell had {X} in its mana cost, include the value chosen for that X when determining how much mana to produce. For example, if you counter a spell that costs {X}{R} with X equal to 5, you'll produce six mana.","oracle_id":"3673219d-d2b5-43ad-b0c8-58b583491158","published_at":"2013-04-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Your precombat main phase is the main phase that happens immediately after your draw step, not any other main phase.","oracle_id":"3673219d-d2b5-43ad-b0c8-58b583491158","published_at":"2013-04-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If this spell doesn't resolve, none of its effects occur. In particular, it will go to the graveyard rather than to its owner's library.","oracle_id":"613a41b8-0b4f-4995-bf1e-ca41f96e6438","published_at":"2011-06-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Because you follow the spell's instructions in order, you won't be able to draw the same Blue Sun's Zenith that you cast.","oracle_id":"613a41b8-0b4f-4995-bf1e-ca41f96e6438","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the target spell is an illegal target by the time Mana Drain tries to resolve, Mana Drain doesn't resolve. You don't add mana at the beginning of your next main phase. If the target is legal but not countered (most likely because an effect says that the spell can't be countered), you do add mana.","oracle_id":"74d3277a-38e5-4732-afed-084a56148f20","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Mana Drain's delayed triggered ability will usually trigger at the beginning of your precombat main phase. However, if you cast Mana Drain during your precombat main phase or during your combat phase, its delayed triggered ability will trigger at the beginning of that turn's postcombat main phase.","oracle_id":"74d3277a-38e5-4732-afed-084a56148f20","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"For spells with {X} in their mana costs, use the value chosen for X to determine the spell's mana value.","oracle_id":"81fa8e6a-5fb8-43de-802f-df5b985c6a7d","published_at":"2017-09-29","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You may target a spell that can't be countered. When Spell Swindle resolves, the target spell will be unaffected, but you'll still get Treasures.","oracle_id":"81fa8e6a-5fb8-43de-802f-df5b985c6a7d","published_at":"2017-09-29","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the spell has damage divided as it was cast, the division can't be changed, although the targets receiving that damage still can. The same is true of spells that distribute counters.","oracle_id":"8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the spell that's copied has an X whose value was determined as it was cast, the copy will have the same value of X.","oracle_id":"8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the spell that's copied is modal (that is, it says \"Choose one —\" or the like), the copy will have the same mode. A different mode can't be chosen.","oracle_id":"8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The copy is created on the stack, so it's not \"cast.\" Abilities that trigger when a player casts a spell won't trigger. The copy will resolve before the original spell does.","oracle_id":"8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The copy will have the same targets as the spell it's copying unless you choose new ones. You may change any number of the targets, including all of them or none of them. If, for one of the targets, you can't choose a new legal target, then it remains unchanged (even if the current target is illegal).","oracle_id":"8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Twincast can copy any instant or sorcery spell, not just one with targets.","oracle_id":"8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can't choose to pay any alternative or additional costs for the copy. However, effects based on any alternative or additional costs that were paid for the original spell are copied as though those same costs were paid for the copy.","oracle_id":"8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The controller of the countered spell doesn't choose how many cards to draw until the relevant ability resolves. The player may draw 0, 1, or 2 cards. They choose the number before drawing any cards.","oracle_id":"ab1cc360-b9de-48d9-9983-4dfe4a7d2a37","published_at":"2007-09-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Volcanic Fallout can be targeted by spells that try to counter it (such as Countersquall). Those spells will still resolve, but the part of their effect that would counter Volcanic Fallout won't do anything. Any other effects those spells have will work as normal.","oracle_id":"bd6ce147-c991-40ac-b276-65b630fad8b6","published_at":"2009-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Hinder's controller, not necessarily the controller of the countered spell, chooses where the countered spell goes.","oracle_id":"c9db6b94-a7b1-4b93-b454-4dead8f85e34","published_at":"2020-08-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a spell with {X} in its mana cost is countered this way, {X} is the value chosen as the spell was cast.","oracle_id":"e197104f-5382-4cb2-8afe-5ca0594629c2","published_at":"2021-04-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the spell you cast has {X} in its mana cost, you must choose 0 as the value of X.","oracle_id":"e197104f-5382-4cb2-8afe-5ca0594629c2","published_at":"2021-04-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you cast a spell “without paying its mana cost,” you can’t pay any alternative costs. You can, however, pay additional costs, such as kicker costs. If the card has any mandatory additional costs, you must pay those.","oracle_id":"e197104f-5382-4cb2-8afe-5ca0594629c2","published_at":"2021-04-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you target a spell that can’t be countered, like Heated Debate, you won’t counter the spell, but you will get to cast a spell with an equal or lesser mana value.","oracle_id":"e197104f-5382-4cb2-8afe-5ca0594629c2","published_at":"2021-04-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This can be used to cast either face of a modal double-faced card, but only if the face you are casting has an equal or lesser mana value than the target spell.","oracle_id":"e197104f-5382-4cb2-8afe-5ca0594629c2","published_at":"2021-04-16","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
